# ── dependencies
node_modules/
.DS_Store
*.log

# ── third-party source material, deliberately NOT redistributed.
#
# The reference videos are the portfolio work of five working designers
# (@byshubh_, @evanplace, @Kirschberg_, @mthblt, @jittervideo). Rehosting them —
# or contact sheets of their frames — is redistribution, and not ours to do.
#
# What IS committed is everything WE produced from them:
#   refs/specs/*.yaml              our written analysis
#   refs/analysis/*/profile.md     measured shot tables + motion curves
#   refs/analysis/*/motion.csv     per-frame measurements
#   refs/analysis/*/meta.json      dimensions / fps / duration
# That is ~2MB of text and gives a skill user every number without a download.
# `./pipeline/fetch_refs.sh --analyze` rebuilds the videos AND contact sheets
# locally in one command.
refs/raw/
refs/analysis/**/sheet_*.jpg
refs/analysis/**/keys/
refs/analysis/**/keys.jpg
refs/harvest/*.probe
audio/raw/
audio/analysis/

# ── generated assets (regenerate with: python3 pipeline/make_sfx.py)
video/public/sfx/

# ── subscription / restricted-licence audio must never be committed.
# Free To Use, Envato, Artlist, Musicbed and Epidemic all permit use in a
# finished video but forbid redistributing the source file. Only the CC BY track
# (digital-lemonade.mp3) is safe to ship, and it stays.
video/public/ft-*.mp3
audio/freetouse-manifest.json

# ── renders and analysis output
video/out/
out-analysis/
*.mp4
*.mov
*.webm

# The one exception: the finished launch video, linked from the README.
# NOTE: git stores a full new copy of this ~21MB file on every commit. It was
# re-committed 5 times during iteration = 107MB of history. If you rebuild the
# demo, upload it as a GitHub Release asset instead of committing it again.
# See "Updating the demo video" in README.md.
!demo/product-os-launch.mp4

# ── remotion
.remotion/
video/.remotion/
